{
 "name": "happy",
 "integration": "efficientip-solidserver",
 "description": "One space, DHCP and DNS joins on, IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. Proves the native X-IPM auth headers ride every request; that the interleaved free-gap pseudo-row is dropped; that the lease supplies the MAC and client hostname when IPAM has none, its first-time drives firstSeen, and the Fingerbank OS stays an attribute; that an EIP:-prefixed reservation pseudo-MAC is discarded; that the AAAA record's long-form address canonicalizes to the same join key as the IPAM row's compressed form; and that 204 No Content ends a walk without an error. The second ip6_address6_list row carries NO hostaddr column -- only the bare 32-hex-digit ip6_addr the API is believed to expose on some installs -- and must still import via the hex fallback rather than being silently skipped (the IPv6 import is on by default, so a missing hostaddr would otherwise yield zero v6 assets with no warning).",
